2026-10-22T10:17:03.8323100Z see https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/205370
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8324220Z 
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8325410Z Using `clang`, `clang++`, etc., requires a CLT installation at `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools`.
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8327080Z If you don't want to install the CLT, you can write appropriate configuration files pointing to your
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8328470Z SDK at ~/.config/clang.
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8329050Z 
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8329550Z To use the bundled libunwind please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8330620Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8331300Z 
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8331760Z To use the bundled libc++ please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8332970Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/c++ -L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8334650Z Features newer than system libc++ will require the following define to enable
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8335870Z (support for this may be removed in a future major LLVM release):
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8336940Z   CPPFLAGS="-D_LIBCPP_DISABLE_AVAILABILITY"
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8337740Z 
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8338860Z NOTE: You probably want to use the libunwind and libc++ provided by macOS unless you know what you're doing.
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8339260Z 
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8339640Z llvm is keg-only, which means it was not symlinked into /opt/homebrew,
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8340210Z because macOS already provides this software and installing another version in
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8340650Z parallel can cause all kinds of trouble.
2026-10-22T10:17:03.8340890Z 
